  RWAOfferingPool hardening
    collateral: one eBL backs one live offering
      √ refuses a second offering on an eBL that already backs a live one
      √ frees the eBL when an unsubscribed offering is cancelled, so it can be offered again
      √ releases the pledge when an offering is repaid, so the eBL can move again
      √ prevents owner bypass of the pledge before settlement
      √ stops selling shares once the eBL is no longer pledged to the pool
    pricing bounds
      √ never lets the oracle price an offering above its target redemption value
      √ REPRICE_DOWN has to lower the price
      √ allows a recovery: an OPEN action may raise a repriced offering again, up to the target
      √ rejects an out-of-range risk level at the oracle and a zero pool
    settlement
      √ refuses proofs and settlement for an offering nobody subscribed to
      √ lets only the owner correct a mistaken importer payment, and keeps the audit trail
      √ validates a correction
      √ records the departure proof and the oracle / token wiring in the event log
    cancelOffering
      √ is owner-only and needs an existing offering
      √ cannot cancel an offering that already has subscribers
      √ works from Open, Repriced and Paused, also during a global emergency stop (39ms)
      √ rejects a second cancel and any state that is not cancellable
    documented limitation
      √ subscribe records an amount owed but holds no funds (no payment leg yet)

